s vasoconstriction  role now it is believed  that vasoconstriction caused by  thromboxane could be the underlying  cause  of prince metals and genome or  any kind of cardiac inflammatory disease  one of the  leading role could be played by  thromboxanes  now let me tell you that in your diet if  you have sufficient amount of omega-3  fatty acids  then the thromboxin that is generated  would be  different so if you have too much of  omega-3 fatty acids  then thromboxane a3 is generated instead  of  a2 while a2 is a potent vasoconstrictor  a3 is less potent and that is why the  vasoconstriction mediated aberrant  effects are less  if your diet contains omega-3 fatty acid  if you want to know more about omega-3  fatty acids  and its health benefit click on the link  in the eye button  now let me tell you vessel constriction  effect of thromboxine could be a  feature of many diseases such as  cardiac diseases like ischemia  reperfusion  disease and also hepatic inflammation  and acute hepatotoxicity  underlying all these disease it is  believed that thromboxane is playing a  key role in this pathophysiology  now thromboxane inhibitors are really  important to treat these kind of  diseases  and you can understand at a molecular  level where thromboxane inhibitors could  potentially work  first of all it can work at  cyclooxygenase level  so by blocking cyclooxygenase specific  uh substances such as aspirin  can block the production of thromboxane  other than that thromboxane selective  synthesis inhibitor can also inhibit  thromboxane a synthesis the red limiting  step of thromboxane  biosynthesis process and there could be  other inhibitors which are  antagonist of thromboxane receptor which  prevents from boxing a2 to bind to their  receptor and thereby prevent from  unboxing signaling  so these are few ways by which  thromboxane can be controlled or the  effect of thromboxane could be  moderated so i hope this video was  informative enough if you like this  video give